-- title:
--   Noetherian local λ-node ring of dimension 2 at (l,l^q)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \neq 2$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, and let $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $l \in k$ satisfy $l^{q^2} = l$, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$; write $A_0 = \mathrm{coeffSubring}\,A\,K = A \cap K$, with reduction $\mathrm{redRestrict}\,\mathrm{red}\,K \colon A_0 \to k$ obtained from $\mathrm{red}$ by restriction. Assume given $x \in A_0$ reducing to $l$, and $\varpi \in A_0$ such that an element $c \in A_0$ reduces to $0$ if and only if $c \in \varpi A_0$. Consider the subring $R$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ consisting of those Laurent series $f$ for which there are $r, s \in A_0[X_0, X_1]$ with $s$ not vanishing at $(l, l^q)$ after reduction of its coefficients and $f \cdot \mathrm{lambdaEval}(s) = \mathrm{lambdaEval}(r)$, where $\mathrm{lambdaEval}$ is the $A_0$-algebra map sending coefficients to constant Laurent series, $X_0$ to the series $\mathrm{lambdaModC}$ and $X_1$ to its level-$q$ expansion $\mathrm{lambdaNModC}$. Then $R$ is Noetherian, is a local ring, has $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} R = 2$, and, for any local-ring structure on $R$, its maximal ideal is the ideal generated by the three elements $\mathrm{lambdaEval}(\varpi)$, $\mathrm{lambdaEval}(X_0 - x)$ and $\mathrm{lambdaEval}(X_1 - x^q)$.
--
--   This identifies the local ring of the level-two ($\lambda$-coordinate) model of the modular curve attached to $\Gamma_0(q) \cap \Gamma(2)$, descended to a number field $K$, at the point with coordinates $(l, l^q)$ on the branch locus: it is a two-dimensional Noetherian local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the uniformiser $\varpi$ together with the two coordinate translations $\lambda - x$ and $\lambda_q - x^q$. It underlies the subsequent analysis of this node ring, including the description of its completion as a crossing model and the identification of maximal ideals and level-two coordinate values.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LambdaNodeLocalized_isNoetherianRing_isLocalRing_lambdaLocalizedAtPoint_coeffSubring.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_LambdaNodeLocalized
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_NodeDescent

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
